epresent the line passing through the origin and parallel to the vector $[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince ${e}^{t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions move away from the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ \n\nAmong the given options, the only phase portrait satisfying these conditions is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069697/assets/904ec8bfe5c8f1b9a63becd782c82da68ef2a70894368418c3710d09bc029db1.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-333270/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "371d99ed-a060-51da-8f0f-7b38a0267bb7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-333270"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-333271/selection/78b0d5a347ce51a3e3397f3f3a7fbd77f86e82b8f481c7db77255bc1c040a408" :answer/id #uuid "b8757a1c-074a-5a92-8f33-c5d98f1b72c8" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069697/assets/c46568f3173dfeaab6e33e83269262e8692f13e245a42983ba1a9d4302ec5357.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333271/selection/678cf576a5294e2af6d1a0dc47f59056b44b24ed3cce24b911fa2c58309361b0" :answer/id #uuid "b5bd9952-4be7-5e1e-a41a-6611d4dc4c2a" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069697/assets/bffb2f815cc5a7db0c521054006aa834b17071f5dd33a97fe977e5d118b771be.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333271/selection/931aea7c7b3cb46c24869c1b115039040f5cb1d6974e2d64e9018fe9a9043ef5" :answer/id #uuid "2734678e-36de-5258-8e41-27219597a7b7" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069697/assets/eba955015a4b919c65dc24facb0baa6e745df134feac32feeae07c99